
Lakehead Students Shop — How to Run
Requirements:
- Java JDK
- Python
- MySQL Server
- Gson and MySQL Connector/J JAR files in the lib folder

make sure you have MYSQL and the loginsystem database is working: If it is not use this code:
CREATE TABLE accounts (
    id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    username VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL UNIQUE, email VARCHAR(254) NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    password_hash VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
); 

Step 1: Install Python needed stuff

Open a terminal in the project folder and run:

python -m pip install -r requirements.txt

Step 2: Start the Python Backend

In the first terminal, run this to start up the flask:

python backend/app.py

Keep this terminal running and open a new terminal.

Step 3: Compile Java

Open another terminal in the project folder and run:

javac -cp ".;lib/*" -d . main.java AccountCreation/*.java

Step 4: Run the Application

java -cp ".;lib/*" main

The login screen should open. You can log in or create an account.

After successfully logging in, the marketplace will open.

Note:
MySQL handles user accounts, while Python Flask and SQLite handle marketplace listings. Keep the Flask backend running while using the application.
